#. module: sale_order_type_automation
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_sale_order_type_automation
msgid ""
".. |company| replace:: ADHOC SA\n"
"\n"
".. |company_logo| image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ingadhoc/maintainer-tools/master/resources/adhoc-logo.png\n"
"   :alt: ADHOC SA\n"
"   :target: https://www.adhoc.com.ar\n"
"\n"
".. |icon| image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ingadhoc/maintainer-tools/master/resources/adhoc-icon.png\n"
"\n"
".. image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/license-AGPL--3-blue.png\n"
"   :target: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl\n"
"   :alt: License: AGPL-3\n"
"\n"
"==========================\n"
"Sale Order Type Automation\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"#. Add to sale order type this options to be executed automatically on sale order confirmation and picking confimation:\n"
"\n"
"    * Create / Validate Invoice\n"
"      * New domain to filter invoices for automatic validation. So, if this filter does NOT find the invoices, they stay in drafts status.\n"
"    * Create / Validate Payment\n"
"    * Confirm picking and products transfer (only on sale order confirmation)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Integration with Account Background Post\n"
"========================================\n"
"\n"
"When ``account_background_post`` is installed (optional), the invoice validation can be deferred\n"
"instead of blocking the operation:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Error traceability.** When the background post cron cannot validate an invoice generated by\n"
"   this automation, the error is logged on the source sale order chatter (the order is resolved\n"
"   through the invoice lines), notifying its internal followers. The invoice keeps a pointer to\n"
"   that order, so a draft invoice always says where its error is.\n"
"\n"
"2. **The order is not confirmed if the invoice fails.** The whole confirmation is aborted, so\n"
"   nothing is left half done: no confirmed order hiding the failure and no invoice left as posted\n"
"   without number nor document type. The user gets a *Confirm anyway* call to action that confirms\n"
"   the order leaving the invoice marked to be validated by the background post cron.\n"
"\n"
"   The error is logged on the order through a separate database connection, so the trace survives\n"
"   the rollback. Being a separate connection, it only sees what is already committed: an order\n"
"   created in the very same transaction that confirms it (an API call doing both at once) is not\n"
"   there yet, so that error travels only in the message the user gets.\n"
"\n"
"   Aborting is the behaviour up to v18. The flows that cannot be torn down (the batch run, which\n"
"   already committed) or that deferred the validation on purpose (API, background post) keep logging\n"
"   the error and confirming the order.\n"
"\n"
"3. **A deferred invoice always says so.** Whenever an invoice is left in draft to be validated in\n"
"   background, both the order and the invoice get a note with the reason, and the invoice points to\n"
"   the order, where the error is. A draft invoice is never a mystery.\n"
"\n"
"4. **Transfers.** The same call to action (*Validate anyway*) is offered when the invoice automation\n"
"   triggered by a transfer validation fails. When validating more transfers than the background post\n"
"   batch size (system parameter ``account_background_post.batch_size``, 20 by default), the invoices\n"
"   are directly created to be validated in background, so a big batch is never blocked by the\n"
"   invoice validation. That decision is not asked but it is never silent: the user also gets a\n"
"   notification when the transfers are validated.\n"
"\n"
"Without ``account_background_post`` there is nothing to defer to, so there is no call to action:\n"
"the confirmation is still aborted and the user gets the plain error, exactly as in v18.\n"
"\n"
"Installation\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"To install this module, you need to:\n"
"\n"
"#. Just install\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"To configure this module, you need to set automation options on sale order type\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"To use this module, you need to:\n"
"\n"
"#. To use must be select an \"sale order type\" who has the configuration that you need, then clik in confirm sale.\n"
"\n"
".. image:: https://odoo-community.org/website/image/ir.attachment/5784_f2813bd/datas\n"
"   :alt: Try me on Runbot\n"
"   :target: http://runbot.adhoc.com.ar/\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
